<title>POLAND: COMPUTERLAND TRADES ON KERB AT PLN 52.</title>
<headline>COMPUTERLAND TRADES ON KERB AT PLN 52.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five kerb transactions in blocks of 100,900, 50,000, 50,000, 21,500 and 16,000 shares in Polish software firm ComputerLand SA at 52 zlotys each were struck on the Warsaw bourse on Tuesday, the bourse said in a statement.</p>
<p>At the regular session Computerland traded at 55 zlotys in a volume of 12,182 shares.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
